Understanding Vacuum Interrupter Testers
Vacuum Interrupter Testers are precision diagnostic instruments specifically engineered to evaluate the operational performance of medium and high-voltage circuit breakers. These sophisticated testers measure critical parameters including contact timing (opening/closing duration, pole synchronization, and contact bounce), coil current characteristics, motor current draw, and mechanical travel dynamics using specialized transducers. These instruments have become indispensable for commissioning vital power infrastructure, implementing preventive maintenance programs, and diagnosing faults in critical switching equipment across utility and industrial facilities.
